<title>GERMANY: Pan-German final Feb cpi inflation 1.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pan-German final Feb cpi inflation 1.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN CPI INFLATION		  Feb 97	Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.4	  +0.5	 +0.5</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.7	  +1.8	 +1.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    118.1	 117.6	116.1</p>
<p> FINAL WEST GERMAN CPI INFLATION  Feb 97	Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.3 (+0.4) +0.5	 +0.5</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr change (pct)		 +1.7 (+1.8) +1.9	 +1.4</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    115.6	 115.2	113.7</p>
<p> EAST GERMAN CPI INFLATION	 Feb 97	 Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)	 +0.4	  +0.7	 +0.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year			    +1.7	  +1.7	 +2.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		    137.5	 136.9	134.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets.  </p>
<p>The Office gave the following details on pan-German CPI:</p>
<p>					    Mth/mth	     Yr/yr</p>
<p>					Feb 97  Jan 97    Feb 97  Jan 97</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco	     +0.2    +0.9	+1.2    +1.5</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes		    unch    -0.2	+0.6    +0.6</p>
<p> Rents &amp; energy		     unch    +0.8	+2.8    +3.2</p>
<p> Of which: rents		    +0.3    +0.6	+2.8    +2.8</p>
<p>	     energy excl. fuel    -1.1    +1.5	+3.0    +4.8</p>
<p> Furniture, household goods     +0.1    unch	+0.5    +0.5</p>
<p> Health and body care goods     +0.9    +0.1	+2.3    +1.8</p>
<p> Traffic and news transmission  +0.1    +0.3	+0.8    +1.0</p>
<p> Education, leisure goods	 unch    +1.9	+2.5    +2.7</p>
<p> Personal equipment, others     +4.0    -1.2	+2.4    +1.3</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
